# FACTORY (the author, 2026-10-05): `@: h f(a)` receives a factory's result; this row wrote `h: f a` until then.
# Item 739: at the root a held callable's call passes the arguments its header declares; a
# header of two formals called with one actual is refused, located, rather than run with a
# missing argument.  Mutant: no count check -- the refusal is no longer the located one.
fn: makePair (int: n) fn: (int: x; int: y) int
    fn: pairN (int: x; int: y) int
        return: x + y + n
    return: pairN

@: p5 makePair(5)
int: a (p5: 1)
sendMessage: exit(exit_code: a; stdout: ""; stderr: "")
return
